From 2abf2bfde6c89963f3b590b08406c35a5b75387a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 14:59:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Issue native control leaves from the platform API primary

The existing native CA can be held as admin-signed platform credentials
(NATIVE_CA_KEY, NATIVE_CA_CERT): sealed to the primary, replicated only as
AEAD under the group key, archived with the key escrowed to the admin
recovery keys. The primary verifies each member's actual serving boot
(bound config through HOST_DATA, the unchanged measured-control verifier,
the original registry, a fresh platform host policy decision with the
verified chip), signs the existing 7-day leaf profile in-process from the
member's public key only, and installs it through the member's pinned
install endpoint. Admission is decided again and a majority commit is
required right before every install; leadership loss, credential
replacement or removal, and stop end the run and its connections.

The role drops every NATIVE_CA_* name at the relay child's final
environment boundary, rewrites credential files to exactly the current set,
serves its public bound config read-only, and counts an archive only when a
sink holds both the snapshot and the recovery envelope. The CLI keeps its
openssl issue as the offline admin fallback; its request, pin and install
functions move to a library with no main check, and every body-bearing
request now requires a valid pin.
